---

## 1. Clean Architecture Layer Boundaries (Non-Negotiable)

Layer dependency direction is strictly:
```text
Transport -> Application -> Domain <- Infrastructure
```

- **Domain Layer (`internal/.../domain`)**:
  - Contains pure Go business entities, domain errors, and consumer-owned repository interfaces.
  - NEVER import `database/sql`, ORMs (`gorm`), HTTP libraries (`net/http`, `fiber`, `gin`), or transport protocols.
  - NEVER import Infrastructure or Transport layers.
- **Application Layer (`internal/.../service`)**:
  - Contains business use cases and orchestrates domain logic.
  - Consumes repository interfaces defined in Domain or Application.
  - NEVER import concrete database adapters or transport frameworks.
- **Infrastructure Layer (`internal/.../repository`, `internal/platform`)**:
  - Implements repository interfaces using SQL/driver libraries (`sqlc`, `pgx`, `database/sql`).
  - NEVER import Transport.
- **Transport Layer (`internal/.../transport`)**:
  - Handles incoming HTTP, gRPC, and WebSocket requests.
  - Translates transport DTOs into domain entities and invokes Application services.
  - NEVER execute direct database queries in handlers.

---

## 2. Guarded Comment Regions & Code Splicing

Loy isolates generated scaffolding and developer-owned logic using managed comment regions:
```go
// loy:region:<name>
// Edits must stay within this block
// loy:endregion
```

- **DO NOT** delete, corrupt, or rename `// loy:region:...` or `// loy:endregion` markers.
- **DO NOT** nest comment regions.
- If comment regions are corrupted, run `loy upgrade` or `loy check --format agent` to diagnose and repair.

---

## 3. Explicit Dependency Wiring

- Loy strictly prohibits dynamic reflection DI containers (`uber/dig`, `google/wire`).
- All dependencies must be wired explicitly using Go constructors (`New...`) in `internal/app/wiring.go`.
- Package-level mutable variables (`var DB *sql.DB`) are forbidden.

---

## 4. Verification & Quality Gates

Before finishing any task, external agents MUST execute:
```bash
# Verify architectural boundaries and obtain self-healing prompts
loy check --format agent

# Run standard verification suite
make check || go test -v -race ./...
```
